---
layout: base.njk
title: The h5p-author skill · Missing Elements
description: The h5p-author skill's zips to install, and the files its build fetches where npm cannot be reached, each at its full address.
# No script but the site's: base.njk writes the policy first in <head>, and the color-scheme script
# is added to script-src by its hash at build (eleventy.config.js).
csp: "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'"
---
{#- No page of the site links here since 2026-11-13, when its prompts stopped sending a chat to read
    the skill from this page: the skill is installed, which is the guide's first step. The page
    stays for what names its address: the skill's route 3, and the copies of it already installed,
    which take the build tool's and the bundles' addresses from it where npm cannot be reached (as
    Grok built on 2026-11-13). The zips are served from this folder too. Its text files are not:
    the zips carry them, and a chat with the text alone, which read them here until 0.9.7, is one
    the skill is no longer offered to (the owner, 2026-11-15). -#}
{#- Every address is written out whole, as its link's text too: a chat's fetch tool may open only
    the addresses it has seen in full, and a relative link is none. -#}
{%- set base = site.url + "/h5p/skill/" -%}
{%- set bundlesBase = site.url + "/h5p/bundles/" -%}
{% include "topbar.njk" %}

<main class="skill wrap" id="main">
  <header class="docs-header">
    <h1>The h5p-author skill</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Its zips to install, and the files its build fetches where npm cannot be reached, each at its
      full address.
    </p>
    {#- A person opens this address too, to see what a prompt sends their chat to: they are told
        what it is, and where the pages for them are. -#}
    <blockquote class="for-person">
      <p>
        <strong>For a person reading this:</strong> the page is written for an AI chat. To install
        the skill, follow
        <a href="{{ site.url }}/h5p/create-with-ai/#install">{{ site.url }}/h5p/create-with-ai/#install</a>.
        The page that makes an activity is
        <a href="{{ site.url }}/h5p/build/">{{ site.url }}/h5p/build/</a>.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      These are the files of h5p-author {{ skill.version }}, the release the build page at
      <a href="{{ site.url }}/h5p/build/">{{ site.url }}/h5p/build/</a> runs. The skill's text is in
      the zips, and on
      <a href="https://github.com/missing-elements/h5p-offline-player/tree/main/skills/h5p-author">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </header>

  {#- The sections are drawn as the build page's timeline (site.css). The lists are drawn without
      bullets, and Safari then reads one as a list only if it is told. -#}
  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
    <h2 id="install-heading"><span class="step-marker"><span class="step-number">1</span></span> Install the skill</h2>
    <p>
      In an agent with a terminal:
      <code>npx skills add missing-elements/h5p-offline-player --skill h5p-author</code>. In a chat
      app, from a zip:
    </p>
    <ul class="skill-files" role="list">
      <li><a href="{{ base }}h5p-author.zip">{{ base }}h5p-author.zip</a>: for Claude and Grok</li>
      <li><a href="{{ base }}h5p-author-chatgpt.zip">{{ base }}h5p-author-chatgpt.zip</a>: for ChatGPT's Plugins</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="bundles-heading">
    <h2 id="bundles-heading"><span class="step-marker"><span class="step-number">2</span></span> To build where npm cannot be reached</h2>
    <p>
      The build tool, which runs with Node and nothing installed, and a bundle per content type:
      the libraries a build of that type reads. Fetch the tool and the bundle of the source's own
      type, as the skill says.
    </p>
    <ul class="skill-files" role="list">
      {%- for file in skill.bundles %}
      <li><a href="{{ bundlesBase }}{{ file }}">{{ bundlesBase }}{{ file }}</a>
        {%- if file == "h5p-author.mjs" %}: the build tool{% endif %}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

</main>

{%- set footIssues = site.github ~ "/h5p-offline-player/issues" %}
